	"edfiCedsDerivedPlugin": {
		// THE DERIVED LINES. Every one PINS its own store: the derived producer must never open the crosswalk's
		// decision store, and the surest way to guarantee that is for it not to know the path (RULING 11.5).
		// The scoring harness is the ONLY reader of the crosswalk store in this order, and it reads by path,
		// read-only, after the fact.
		//
		// maxJudgmentCount IS DECLARED HERE AND IS NOT YET INJECTABLE (GRANITE_VALLEY 2026-08-17, raised to the
		// supervisor). RULING 11.12 requires a per-LINE maxJudgmentCount and says "the runner refuses a line
		// without it". The declaration and the runner's refusal are implemented. What is NOT implemented is the
		// cap actually reaching the framework: the only per-line channel is the command line, build.js owns flag
		// parsing, and build.js is a SEAM FILE this order may not touch. So the framework's ceiling remains its
		// data default (MAX_JUDGMENT_COUNT_PER_RUN = 20,000) until that is ruled. The numbers below are a
		// CONTRACT THE RUNNER ENFORCES AT THE BOUNDARY, not yet a ceiling inside the run - and saying so here is
